      "pressure_range_status": "theoretical",
      "determination_method": "theoretical",
      "notes": "Static-lattice 0 K DFT parameterization of the ideal cubic Pm-3m (Glazer a0a0a0) CaSiO3 perovskite branch. The paper finds this branch dynamically unstable at all investigated pressures, so this is a theoretical reference curve and not a stable ambient phase. Table 2 reports V0/Z; Pm-3m has Z=1, so 44.579 A^3 is also the conventional cubic-cell volume (a0=3.54577 A). All three BM3 coefficients were fitted; no parameter uncertainties, covariance, fit weights, or underlying E(V) rows are published. The Table 2 footnote estimates calculation uncertainty as about 20 meV per molecule, an energy-scale estimate rather than an EOS-coefficient error. The distinct Pm-3m BM4 fit and all eight phase-specific low-symmetry BM3/BM4 pairs are now represented as executable sibling records on the appropriate material cards.",
      "reference": {
        "authors": ["Caracas", "Wentzcovitch", "Price", "Brodholt"],
        "year": 2005,
        "title": "CaSiO3 perovskite at lower mantle pressures",
        "source": "Geophys. Res. Lett.",
        "volume": "32",
        "locator": "L06306",
        "doi": "10.1029/2004GL022144"
      }
    },
    {
      "identifier": "ca_perovskite_kawai_2014_vinet_mgd_3",
