        "source_note": "The final article selects a 1000 K reference because cubic CaSiO3 is unstable at 300 K, plots the Vinet-MGD compression curves, and reports V0=46.17 A^3/formula unit, K0=203.95 GPa in the abstract, K0'=4.76, fixed theta0=1100 K, gamma0=1.576, and q=0.96. Its Table 1 isochors numerically support the abstract K0 despite the 203.5 GPa value extracted from Table 2. Section 2's printed 300-1500 K simulation range conflicts with Figure 2's calculated 1000-4000 K points.",
